# ...and KEEP every XML deliberately placed under docs/ as evidence.
#
# F36 cost this project EIGHT cited evidence captures: a document pointed at an
# artifact that `*.xml` above had silently swallowed, so the citation resolved to
# nothing. The narrow per-directory negations above are the shape of fix that
# caused it -- each new audit directory needs someone to REMEMBER to add a line
# here, and the failure is invisible (the file is simply absent; `git status`
# says nothing, and `git add` on it succeeds with no error and stages nothing).
#
# docs/ holds documentation and evidence, never build output, so an XML written
# there was put there on purpose. The generated-docs directories below
# (docs/_build/, docs/html/, docs/latex/) are excluded as DIRECTORIES and git
# does not descend into an excluded directory, so this does not re-admit them.
!docs/**/*.xml

